Not really; lots of players have games going on more than one server. 
We certainly encourage folks to switch servers if they have a game 
crash, since logging back into the same server would risk wiping out the 
recoverable info from the crashed game.

> b) would this screw up my streak on the server? IE, I first ascended a Sam, 
> and then started the barb game. If I ignored the barb game for now and 
> ascended a rogue next would the tourny script consider it a streak?

Streaks are based on when the control server receives the logs of 
completed games from the game servers.  As the logs are imported into 
the database (every 10 minutes) they're tagged with the sequence in 
which they are imported; it's this sequence that determines streaks.

This does mean that you can exploit this to build artificial streaks, by 
running a game up to just before ascension on each server and then 
ascending them all.  This would only affect the Best of 13 trophy and 
the "with Bells On" modifier for the Recognition trophies, since nothing 
else really cares about sequence.  It's not a _huge_ problem, though, 
since I can count the number of players who could pull 6 ascensions in 
one month on my fingers and if last year is any indication, 6 wouldn't 
be nearly enough to win ...

The best solution to this is probably to have the games servers be ntp 
clients of the control server, then use the starting time recorded by 
the xlog patch to determine sequencing.  That's in the feature list 
assigned to next year, though.

